{"title":"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which of the following numbers divide exactly into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/7/1778ef229ce9f6161f16c022b5ac481562d0f0aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 + \\sqrt{49}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"21\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/4/c34c6500d3f58525cc92c7d79cd6146b8a3ac649.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 3 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 4 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 5 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 7 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Simplifying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/7/1778ef229ce9f6161f16c022b5ac481562d0f0aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 + \\sqrt{49}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"21\" />, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/a/caa064b758e971ea8229774afa5595397a5d3b97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 + \\sqrt{49} = 15 + 7 = 22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"192\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Splitting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d111a5e00ee5ea6700bb629994dc629874c505b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> into its prime factorization, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/1/8b1a22dbff35f958bb5bd79d96ceff780b94f853.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22 = 2 \\times 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>We can now clearly see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/c/dfc1f49dce8a822c719603dab4c2e631a317af71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(E) } 11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" /> goes into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d111a5e00ee5ea6700bb629994dc629874c505b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal\">1999 CEMC Pascal</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Answer_Key\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1999 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_1\" titl